   "level": 3,
   "title": "When to use 「あげる」"
  }
 ],
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "When to use 「あげる」"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Vocabulary"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "1. あげる (ru-verb) - to give; to raise"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "2. 私【わたし】- me; myself; I"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "3. 友達【とも・だち】- friend"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "4. プレゼント - present"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "5. これ - this"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "6. 先生【せん・せい】- teacher"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "7. 車【くるま】- car"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "8. 買う【か・う】(u-verb) - to buy"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "9. 代わり【か・わり】- substitute"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "10. 行く【い・く】(u-verb) - to go"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "11. 学生【がく・せい】- student"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "12. 父【ちち】- father"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "13. いい (i-adj) - good"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "14. こと - event, matter"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "15. 教える【おし・える】(ru-verb) - to teach; to inform"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "「あげる」 is the Japanese word for \"to give\" seen from the speaker's point of view. You must use this verb when you are giving something or doing something for someone else."
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "1. 私が友達にプレゼントをあげた。\nI gave present to friend."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "2. これは先生にあげる。\nI'll give this to teacher."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "In order to express the giving of a favor (verb) you must use the ever useful te-form and then attach 「あ げる」. This applies to all the other sections in this lesson as well."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "1. 車を買ってあげるよ。\nI'll give you the favor of buying a car."
  }
 ]
}